  "context": "## Surviving Capability: Why the Field Celebrates What the Theory Condemns\nWhy the field celebrates what the theory condemns. The practitioner’s notes praise the informal taxi swarm, the analog protocol, the constraint-born workaround — exactly the off-map divergence the theory treats as pathology. It looks like the corpus contradicts itself. It does not, and the answer is in three things I lived: two transport systems — one that repaired its map, one that froze — and Uber, which proves the point by changing the technology and nothing else. The field never celebrated the inefficiency. It celebrated the capability that had not yet been lost.\nEtiquetas: Casos de uso y aplicaciones 15.39%; Economía, costes y liquidez 15.39%; Empresa y gestión 15.38%; Evidencia, procedencia y atribución 23.08%; Memoria, comunidad y territorio 15.38%; Transformación y continuidad operativa 15.38%\nFicha: https://dakleyer.github.io/perspective-beyond/sources/surviving-capability-why-the-field-celebrates-what-the-theory-condemns-u1792/\nDocumento de origen: https://jubap.us/surviving-capability-why-the-field-celebrates-what-the-theory-condemns/\n\n",
